title: The Opposition Coordination Table
subtitle: KO wants discipline; the Left wants cooperation without absorption.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_party_card
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_opposition_coordination_timer <= 0 and left_in_government = 0 and caretaker_government = 0 and ko_seats > 0 and (prime_minister = "Mateusz Morawiecki" or prime_minister = "Beata Szydło" or prime_minister = "Przemysław Czarnek")
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_opposition_coordination_timer = 3
card-image: img/poland/cards/opposition-coordination.webp

= The Opposition Coordination Table

One avoidable procedural defeat has become three. KO proposes a permanent table
for votes, investigations and constitutional bills. Its negotiators assume the
largest opposition party will also set the message.

- @procedural_pact
- @economic_competition
- @democratic_minimum

@procedural_pact
title: Accept a disciplined procedural pact
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Parliament works better; Left independence looks thinner.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: A permanent parliamentary team requires one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; ko_relation += 7; judicial_legitimacy += 2; constitutional_restraint += 2; public_trust += 1; razem_dissent += 3; party_unity -= 1; urban_progressive_support += 1; turnout_readiness += 1; news_headline = "The democratic opposition learns to count votes"

Joint whips stop losing amendments through carelessness. KO briefs the press
first, describes the outcome as its initiative and invites the Left to be
pleased that the substance survived.

- #poland_card_finish

@economic_competition
title: Coordinate procedure, compete openly on economics
subtitle: A sharper Left profile wins attention and worsens the relationship.
on-arrival: left_poll += 0.3; labor_credibility += 4; media_capacity += 1; ko_relation -= 5; public_trust += 1; barons_dissent += 1; workers_support += 2; young_support += 1; news_headline = "The Left challenges KO from the parliamentary rostrum"

You warn KO about votes, then attack its labour and housing record in public.
Nobody can claim the Left disappeared into a democratic bloc. Nobody can claim
the bloc is comfortable either.

- #poland_card_finish

@democratic_minimum
title: Limit the pact to courts, elections and public media
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. A credible constitutional minimum with fewer coalition assumptions.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Legal drafting and monitoring require one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; ko_relation += 4; judicial_legitimacy += 4; constitutional_restraint += 4; progressive_credibility += 1; pis_relation -= 2; razem_dissent -= 1; urban_progressive_support += 1; turnout_readiness += 2; news_headline = "Opposition parties publish a democratic minimum"

The document is narrow enough for Razem and broad enough for constitutional
lawyers. It offers no joint economic programme and therefore postpones the
hardest coalition argument.

- #poland_card_finish
